From 6ffc2fe723789e73629e44c40b539cacb06b0991 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ecogamezz <33791269+ecogamezz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:27:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] WowCraft: combat, life, gifts, water and Minecraft's
 loose things

- combat: WoW's units round us as Minecraft's actor table (hittable stand-ins; friendly ones
  unhittable; innkeepers and general goods vendors as block traders), ore veins, herbs and
  stations as Minecraft nodes; a Minecraft hit as GM `.damage`, scaled by level and health;
  WoW's melee, spells, ticks and lava as Minecraft damage; WoW's own auto-attack stopped; kill
  loot by creature kind
- life: god mode and GM mode off on entering the world; Minecraft's death as ours, the spirit
  released and revived at the graveyard
- gifts: each character's Minecraft inventory, quest rewards (emeralds, gear for our level,
  food, experience), experience as orbs where the kill fell
- water: WoW's water and lava under our feet as Minecraft's
- blocks: dropped items, arrows, cracks, the fishing line and the block outline drawn in WoW
- the view follows Minecraft's field of view, and farclip 500 while flying
- WoW's interface under WowCraft: action bars, Log Out, the cinematic, tutorials, the name
- a stale Minecraft state from an earlier game is dropped, and teleports are numbered per game
- the chat leaves out the answers to the module's own GM commands

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
